# Metrics component observations, 2026-10-12

The separate standard dispatch and percentile candidates passed their source-bound timing and isolated-memory sequences. Neither is selected for production. The standard candidate recorded lower small/large-standard medians but a p95 regression. The percentile candidate recorded a substantially lower single-p95 median but regressions in large standard, all percentiles and all calculations. These are finite component observations, with overlapping ranges in several controls; they establish no statistical significance, whole-product result or universal superiority.

The complete arithmetic/raw-data report is `measurement-review.json`, SHA-256 `e6bbe2b3f6d4c55ad7eadc4fe466d83de42b367fb7c993c1539d8691a16e7e3c`. `results/timing-summary.csv` and `memory-summary.csv` retain all medians/minima/maxima; JSON also retains every seven-sample vector. Original raw 105-child receipts and the 840 raw memory worker/observer logs remain unchanged. Six static SVG/PNG figures are bound to exact input/source/runtime identities in `results/figures-validation.json` and were visually inspected. A separate Python statistics replay checked 5,790 summary groups, all medians/minima/maxima/paired differences, sequential unique sample identities and figure fingerprints without executing reducers.

## Quiet coordination and durations

Root established and explicitly closed a coordinated interval from **20:26:14.000 to 20:38:55.000 UTC**. Root reported that it and the other agents performed no tests, builds, browser interactions, publication or source scans during this interval. Each sequence had a fresh explicit timestamp. The acknowledgments and instructions are preserved in four authorization JSON files and `results/quiet-window-close.json`. Unrelated Windows/background work remained uncontrolled; no machine-level isolation is established. Idle app servers continued running. Consolidation, figures and their checks happened after closure, while root resumed other work.

