Timing wrapper intervals were 20:27:05.089–20:28:15.976 and 20:29:09.935–20:30:20.413. The JSON records wrapper and sample intervals distinctly. There were 210 timing children and 210 isolated-memory children, with seven fresh sequential samples per implementation/workload and rotating order. All 852,516 fresh/last/retained memory output/cache checks passed. There were **zero actual measurement failures or limit-hit/censored trials**. All owned workers and RSS observers ended before closure. No counts, thresholds, sources or candidates changed during measurement.

## Timing medians and full ranges

Times are milliseconds per call. Brackets contain full seven-process min–max ranges, not confidence intervals. Each trial compares released original, frozen baseline and its own separate candidate. All three implementations were loaded in timing children for correctness, so their incidental memory values cannot establish isolated implementation memory. Lower times are faster.

